(139, 1, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The </span><strong>Department of Science &amp; Technology</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> offers the </span><strong>Bachelor of Science in Information Technology (BSc.IT)</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> program, aimed at developing skilled professionals in the field of modern computing and digital technologies. The department focuses on providing a balanced combination of </span><strong>theoretical knowledge and practical application</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in various areas of information technology.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The BSc.IT curriculum includes subjects such as </span><strong>programming, database management systems, networking, web development, software engineering, cybersecurity, and data management</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Through well-equipped computer laboratories, practical sessions, and project-based learning, students gain hands-on experience with the latest software tools and technologies.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The department is equipped with modern computer laboratories, updated software tools, and experienced faculty members who guide students in academic as well as professional development. Various activities such as </span><strong>seminars, workshops, technical events, internships, and industry interactions</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> are organized to keep students updated with current technological trends.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The BSc.IT program under the Department of Science &amp; Technology prepares students for careers in </span><strong>software development, IT services, system administration, networking, and data analysis</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, while also providing a strong foundation for higher education and research in Information Technology and related fields.</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-03-24 00:00:00'),
