(175, 1, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><strong>Established - 1972</strong></p>\n<p>Established in 1972, the Department of Hindi has been a pioneer department of Maniben Nanavati Women&rsquo;s College, Mumbai. Right from inception, it was headed by <strong>Dr. Pragnya Shukla</strong>. She did many activities in multiple spheres during her long tenure of 37 years. She was superannuated in 2008.</p>\n<p><strong>Dr. Ravindra Katyayan</strong> took over the charge of the Hindi Department in 2009. He raised the Department of Hindi to further heights by organizing many national and international seminars, conferences, and workshops in collaboration with ICSSR, NCPSL, CHD, MSHSA, and many others.</p>\n<p>He also established international and national MoUs with institutions such as <strong>Guang Dong University of Foreign Studies (GDUFS)</strong>, China; <strong>Shenzhen University</strong>, China; <strong>Udayana University</strong>, Bali; <strong>Lincoln University</strong>, Malaysia; <strong>Global Hindi Foundation</strong>, Singapore; <strong>Shri Mallikarjun College</strong>, Goa; and <strong>Yatha Katha Film and Literature Festival</strong>, Mumbai. He conducted many activities and conferences in China, Indonesia, Cambodia, and India.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 237, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
