(211, 1, 7, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Department of Gujarati, established in 1972, is dedicated to preserving and promoting the rich literary heritage and cultural essence of the Gujarati language. It strives to develop students&rsquo; linguistic competence, literary appreciation, and creative expression through a balanced blend of academic and co-curricular activities. The department actively nurtures reading, writing, speaking, and analytical skills while instilling pride in the mother tongue.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A key highlight of the department is the celebration of Vishva Gujarati Bhasha Divas on 21st February, which creates awareness about the importance of language preservation. Guest lectures by eminent scholars and writers provide valuable insights into Gujarati literature and contemporary trends. The department also strengthens academic collaboration through MoUs by organizing workshops and conferences.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Extension activities form an integral part of the department&rsquo;s vision, through which students develop social responsibility alongside academic growth. Educational visits to literary institutions, libraries, and cultural centers further enhance experiential learning.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rooted in tradition yet open to innovation, the department continues its journey like an ever-flowing stream of words, nurturing minds and carrying forward the legacy of the Gujarati language with pride, purpose, and poetic grace.</span></p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-03-24 00:00:00'),
(212, 2, 7, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
