(247, 1, 9, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><strong>Date of Commencement of Dept.: 1972</strong></p>\n<div class=\"dept\">\n<p>Every year this Department rolls out graduates with a strong commitment to contribute to society in their own capacities. Students from diverse academic and social backgrounds &ndash; from economically challenged minorities to the ones who wish to transform their lives to become self-sufficient and move towards upward social mobility; from the mediocre to bright ones, from average to weaker ones opt for Sociology as their Discipline Component.</p>\n<p>The Department embraces them all and offers various platforms of equity to excel in academics, research, soft skills, employment opportunities and community work. Be it field work, surveys or innovations in student-centric teaching-learning methods, internships or research-based studies, the Department offers endless opportunities to students to excel in a wide range of activities.</p>\n<p>The outcomes are indeed rewarding- many of them who are first generation college and at time school goers bring us pride when they excel in academics and win prizes in co-curricular and extra-curricular, research and other competitions. Overcoming all kinds of challenges at familial, community, social and most importantly at financial levels, these students complete their graduation. After completing their graduation, students opt for progression not only in the field of sociology but also for studying law, education, management, women&rsquo;s studies and others. Our alumni are lawyers, teachers, entrepreneurs, HR Representatives.</p>\n</div>', '1', 1, '', 0, 237, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(248, 2, 9, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(261, 16, 9, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(265, 152, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(266, 1, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The BA Psychology program is highly regarded for its strong faculty, practical training approach, and supportive environment for women. Some of the key features include:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Syllabus:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> The curriculum builds a strong foundation in core psychological principles while equipping students with the insight &amp; skills to navigate the evolving landscape of human interaction with AI.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Excellent Lab Facilities:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> The college boasts one of the most&nbsp;well-equipped psychology labs in the state, allowing students to gain hands-on experience with psychological testing and assessments.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Qualified and Supportive Faculty:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> The psychology department is known for its&nbsp;highly qualified, experienced, and dedicated teachers&nbsp;who are passionate about the subject. They employ interactive teaching methods and provide personal attention to ensure students grasp both theoretical and practical concepts.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Conduction of Workshops &amp; Events: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The department regularly organizes events for World Suicide Prevention Day &amp; World Mental Health Day that include reaching out to the community for awareness and psychoeducation. Activities such as research competitions enhance learning beyond the classroom. Guest lectures by renowned psychologists are also a key feature.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Great Internship Spaces:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Internships are a key part of the curriculum, with&nbsp;opportunities provided from the second year onwards. Students have secured internships at reputable organizations that have built their professional and subject specific skills.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><strong>Research Training: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Interested students receive in-depth guidance and training in research enabling them to win prominent research competitions at the national level.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><strong>Diverse pedagogy:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> The department follows different methods of instruction and evaluation including lectures, videos, field visits, experts special lectures, seminars and commemoration of days related to well-being and mental health.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In summary, MNWC offers a comprehensive BA Psychology program that combines academic rigor with practical exposure, all within an empowering environment for women. We ensure students think, observe, assess and critically evaluate various psychological processes and manifested behaviour across all contexts.</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /><br /></p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-03-24 00:00:00'),
(267, 2, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(280, 16, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 237, '2025-12-13 00:00:00'),
(284, 1, 11, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The </span><strong>M.A. in Psychology</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a two-year postgraduate programme offering a rigorous and contemporary curriculum designed to build strong theoretical foundations and applied competencies. The program has two specialisations - Clinical and Counseling Psychology.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Programme Highlights</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>Comprehensive Curriculum</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NEP 2020 based curriculum. Advanced courses in Clinical, Counseling, Cognitive, Social, and Applied Psychology with Research Methodology, Statistics, and Dissertation.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>Qualified Staff- </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The curriculum is supported by experienced faculty with strong research orientation and field expertise, ensuring a balanced approach to academic excellence and applied learning.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>Well-Equipped Psychology Laboratory</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">-Hands-on training in psychological testing, assessment, and experimental methods.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>Internship &amp; Field Exposure</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Structured internships in hospitals, NGOs, schools, and organizations to ensure real-world experience. Receive training in Psychological Assessment &amp; Testing</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>Emphasis on Ethics, Plagiarism &amp; AI Awareness</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">:</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> S</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">tudents are guided on the appropriate and ethical use of Artificial Intelligence and digital tools in research, assessment, and academic work. The focus is on developing critical thinking, transparency, and accountability while using emerging technologies responsibly in professional psychological settings.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>Academic Excellence</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">- Consistent university toppers and outstanding academic performance.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its focus on high-level applied and active learning experiences that integrate research and professional practice. Students receive comprehensive exposure to Clinical, and Counseling Psychology, combining theoretical understanding with structured practical training.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Through internships in Hospitals, NGOs, educational institutions, and organizational settings, students gain hands-on field experience. The programme also encourages scholarly engagement, guiding students to undertake research projects and present or publish their work at national and international forums.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the PG department of Psychology., we strive to provide a holistic approach to learning that promotes academic growth, professional competence, and ethical responsibility.</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /><br /></p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-03-24 00:00:00'),
