(321, 1, 13, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p class=\"mt-2\">The department of Child Development at Maniben Nanavati Women&rsquo;s College is well equipped with innovative techno-pedagogical abilities that enable learners to work more efficiently with emerging technology. Our professors&rsquo; broad understanding of&nbsp;<strong>early childhood education courses</strong>&nbsp;differentiates us as an institution.</p>\n<p class=\"mt-2\">Department of child development was founded in 1983 at <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #3598db; text-decoration: underline;\"><a style=\"color: #3598db; text-decoration: underline;\" href=\"https://mnwc.edu.in/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Maniben Nanavati Women&rsquo;s College.</strong></a></span></span> Since its inception it has empowered students in life skills and trained students in Early&nbsp;<strong><strong>Childhood Education and Care</strong></strong>. Faculty and Head of the department, Dr. Swati Partani herself is an expert in Multiple Intelligences Theory and students from this department utilizes this theory to understand self and work with preschool children. Department is updated with innovative techno-pedagogical skills, which further empowers the students to work efficiently with evolving technology. Students are rigorously involved in research-based practices in the teaching learning process. Students along with faculty have published research papers in UGC approved journals. Students also study dynamics of adolescents issues, children with special needs, marriage and family conflicts. They learn many coping strategies in mentioned areas. Various Skill development programmes are conducted for the students like Puppet making, Creative development, Excel training, preschool management to enhance vocational skills. Students have become entrepreneurs after completing their course and enrol for&nbsp;<strong><strong>M.Sc. in Human Development</strong></strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong><strong>Early childhood Education post-graduation</strong></strong>. One of the alumni is running her own ISO certified training institute. Others are individually utilizing their training to become financially independent, also working with the preschool sector.</p>\n<p class=\"mt-2\">Not only this, students are trained to give back to the society in the form of extension activities. Teaching and working with the underprivileged students by conducting training programmes in vacations. Their creative teaching learning materials are donated to the preschool from balwadi, refugee camp, and preschool in need.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 237, '2025-11-13 00:00:00'),
(322, 2, 13, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(335, 16, 13, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(340, 1, 14, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Department of Food &amp; Nutrition is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement in the dynamic field of food science and nutrition. Under the leadership of Dr. Shama Chavan, Head of the Department, the department strives to nurture competent professionals equipped with scientific knowledge, practical skills, and social responsibility. The department offers a strong academic foundation combined with experiential learning through practical sessions, workshops, extension activities, and research initiatives. Students are encouraged to develop skills in diet planning, food preparation, food entrepreneurship, and community outreach. This year students from the department participated in ANVESHAN, an Intercollegiate research competition. BITE-DELITE is a unique entrepreneurship activity conducted by the students every year where students sell meals within the campus and earn profit. Every year, the department actively celebrates National Nutrition Month with a series of awareness programs, poster competitions, expert lectures, and demonstrations to promote the importance of balanced diets and healthy lifestyles among students and the community. A flagship initiative of Internal Quality Assurance Cell [IQAC]&nbsp; managed by the department is Project AKSHAYA, through which nutritious and healthy snacks are thoughtfully served to students. This project aims to encourage healthy eating habits, reduce junk food consumption, and create awareness about affordable, nutrient-rich food choices. Through academic excellence and community-oriented programs, the Department of Food &amp; Nutrition continues to promote health, sustainability, and well-being.</span></p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-03-24 00:00:00'),
(341, 2, 14, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(354, 16, 14, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
(359, 1, 15, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Bachelor of Management Studies (BMS) programme is a dynamic, future-focused course designed to shape competent, ethical, and industry-ready management professionals. Blending academic excellence with experiential learning, BMS ensures holistic development through guest lectures, workshops, bridge courses, field visits, industrial exposure, and add-on certifications.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Eminent academicians and industry experts deliver Insightful sessions on professional ethics, entrepreneurship, and management entrance preparation, connecting theory with real-world practice. Skill-driven workshops in employability skills, research methodology, digital tools, resume building, interview techniques, website design, and financial internship orientation enhance students&rsquo; professional readiness.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A dedicated Bridge Course supports students from Arts and Science backgrounds, ensuring a smooth academic transition. Field visits to premier institutions and industries including the National Stock Exchange, Management institutes, nature parks, and manufacturing units offer invaluable practical exposure.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Add-on certifications such as Advanced Excel, Power BI, and Digital Marketing further empower students with cutting-edge competencies, making BMS a gateway to leadership and career excellence.</span></p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-03-24 00:00:00'),
(360, 2, 15, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '', '1', 1, '', 0, 0, '2025-11-12 00:00:00'),
