(447, 1, 18, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Department of Commerce (M.Com) offers specializations in Advanced Management, Accounting &amp; Auditing, and Human Resource Management, standing as a centre of academic excellence with strong industry integration. To educate postgraduates for fast-paced, international business environments, the department places a strong emphasis on research-driven learning, professional competency development, and entrepreneurial leadership development. Students obtain practical experience through research projects in financial reporting, taxation, auditing, financial modelling, compliance, risk management, payroll, and recruitment procedures through organized internships with chartered accountancy firms, financial institutions, corporate finance departments, consulting firms, and HR departments. Industrial trips to prestigious organizations like the National Stock Exchange of India and the Bombay Stock Exchange connect theoretical understanding with practical capital market activities.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Through experienced guest lectures, NET/SET and CA/CMA/CS advice, research workshops, and additional certifications in SPSS, Advanced Excel, GST, and healthcare billing in partnership with Tech Mahindra, the department further enhances professional preparedness.</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For the academic year 2023&ndash;2024, Ms. Adam Tahirah emerged as the overall University Topper in the M.Com program.</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">By giving students the opportunity to plan and oversee company endeavours, the creative \"Financial Report\" program promotes experiential entrepreneurial learning. The department is a centre for advanced commerce education and business alignment thanks to strategic Memorandums of Understanding with reputable organizations that guarantee research collaboration, internships, mentoring, and placement support.</span></p>\n<p><br /><br /><br /><br /></p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-03-24 00:00:00'),
