(1464, 188, 23, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Industry-Relevant Curriculum: </strong>A contemporary NEP-based curriculum covering Cyber Security, Digital Forensics, Programming, Networks, and Cryptography, aligned with current industry practices.</li>\n<li><strong>Academic Excellence with Technical Depth: </strong>Delivered by experienced faculty with domain expertise, ensuring strong conceptual clarity and applied understanding.</li>\n<li><strong>Hands-on Security Training: </strong>Extensive lab-based learning in system security, threat analysis, and foundational forensic techniques using modern tools.</li>\n<li><strong>Application-Driven Learning: </strong>Focus on real-world scenarios, case studies, and problem-solving approaches in cyber security and digital investigations.</li>\n<li><strong>Digital &amp; Analytical Skill Development: </strong>Exposure to data tools, system analysis, and technical platforms supporting security operations.</li>\n<li><strong>Ethics, Cyber Laws &amp; Responsibility: </strong>Strong emphasis on legal frameworks, data privacy, and ethical practices in cyber security.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pathways for Professional Growth: </strong>Prepares students for careers in cyber security, digital forensics, and advanced studies in the field.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its emphasis on practical, investigative, and analytical learning, enabling students to think beyond systems and understand the dynamics of cyber threats and digital evidence. The learning journey progresses from foundational concepts to advanced domains such as ethical hacking, network security, and forensic analysis.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the Department of Cyber Security &amp; Digital Forensics, we aim to develop professionals who are technically proficient, analytically strong, and ethically grounded to address the complex challenges of the digital age.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-05-23 00:00:00'),
(1465, 188, 24, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Future-Ready Curriculum: </strong>NEP-based curriculum covering Programming, Data Science, Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, and mathematical foundations.</li>\n<li><strong>Academic Rigor with Practical Orientation: </strong>Delivered by experienced faculty, ensuring strong fundamentals combined with real-world application.</li>\n<li><strong>Hands-on AI &amp; ML Training: </strong>Practical exposure to data analysis, model building, and machine learning techniques using modern tools and platforms.</li>\n<li><strong>Application-Centric Learning: </strong>Focus on solving real-world problems through data-driven approaches and intelligent systems.</li>\n<li><strong>Exposure to Emerging Technologies: </strong>Introduction to areas such as deep learning, natural language processing, and AI-based applications.</li>\n<li><strong>Ethical &amp; Responsible AI Practices: </strong>Emphasis on fairness, bias, data privacy, and responsible use of AI technologies.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Career &amp; Research Pathways: </strong>Strong foundation for careers in AI, ML, data science, and advanced academic pursuits.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its focus on <strong>experiential and analytical learning</strong>, where students actively work with datasets, develop models, and build intelligent solutions. The curriculum ensures a structured progression from foundational concepts to advanced AI applications.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the Department of Artificial Intelligence &amp; Machine Learning, we aim to nurture innovators who combine technical expertise with critical thinking and ethical responsibility in the field of intelligent systems.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-05-23 00:00:00'),
(1466, 188, 25, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Industry-Aligned Curriculum: </strong>NEP-based curriculum covering Data Analytics, Statistics, Programming, Data Visualization, and Machine Learning.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Strong Academic &amp; Analytical Foundation: </strong>Delivered by experienced faculty, focusing on conceptual clarity and analytical thinking.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Hands-on Data Training: </strong>Practical exposure to data cleaning, analysis, visualization, and interpretation using modern tools.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Application-Oriented Learning: </strong>Real-world datasets, case studies, and analytical projects to build problem-solving skills.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Tools &amp; Technology Exposure: </strong>Training in Excel, Tableau, Power BI, and programming environments for data analysis.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ethics &amp; Data Responsibility:</strong> Focus on data privacy, ethical use of data, and responsible analytics practices.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Career &amp; Growth Opportunities: </strong>Prepares students for roles in data analytics, business intelligence, and further studies.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its focus on <strong>analytical and insight-driven learning</strong>, where students engage deeply with data to identify patterns, trends, and meaningful conclusions. The curriculum progresses from foundational statistics and programming to advanced analytics and predictive modelling.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the Department of Data Science &amp; Data Analytics, we aim to develop professionals who can interpret data effectively, think critically, and contribute meaningfully to data-driven decision-making in a rapidly evolving world.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-05-23 00:00:00'),
(1467, 188, 26, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Globally Aligned Curriculum: </strong>A contemporary NEP-based curriculum covering Financial Accounting, Management Accounting, Taxation, Auditing, and International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS), designed to meet global industry expectations.</li>\n<li><strong>Academic Excellence with Professional Orientation: </strong>Delivered by experienced faculty with strong academic and professional expertise, ensuring conceptual depth along with practical relevance.</li>\n<li><strong>Application-Driven Learning: </strong>Focused on case studies, financial analysis, and real-world business scenarios to build strong decision-making and problem-solving abilities.</li>\n<li><strong>International Perspective in Accounting &amp; Finance: </strong>Understanding of global financial systems, cross-border transactions, and international compliance frameworks.</li>\n<li><strong>Technology-Enabled Learning: </strong>Exposure to accounting software, financial tools, and digital platforms used in modern finance and business environments.</li>\n<li><strong>Ethics, Governance &amp; Professional Integrity: </strong>Emphasis on ethical accounting practices, corporate governance, and regulatory frameworks essential for responsible financial management.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Pathways for Professional Growth: </strong>Strong foundation for pursuing global certifications and advanced studies in accounting, finance, and related domains.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its emphasis on <strong>analytical thinking and professional readiness</strong>, enabling students to interpret financial information, evaluate business performance, and adapt to global accounting practices. The learning experience is designed to move beyond classroom teaching, encouraging application, critical analysis, and industry awareness.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Through a balanced approach of academic rigor and practical exposure, students develop the confidence and competence required to succeed in dynamic financial environments, both in India and internationally.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the Department of Commerce, we are committed to nurturing professionals who combine technical expertise with a global outlook, ethical responsibility, and a strong foundation for lifelong learning.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-05-23 00:00:00'),
(1468, 188, 27, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<ul>\n<li><strong>Industry-Relevant Curriculum: </strong>NEP-based curriculum covering Marketing, Digital Marketing, Social Media Strategies, SEO/SEM, Content Marketing, Analytics, and AI applications in business.</li>\n<li><strong>Academic Excellence with Practical Orientation: </strong>Delivered by experienced faculty with expertise in commerce, marketing, and digital domains, ensuring a balance between theory and application.</li>\n<li><strong>Hands-on Digital Marketing Training: </strong>Practical exposure to campaign planning, content creation, social media management, and performance analysis using modern tools.</li>\n<li><strong>Integration of AI in Marketing: </strong>Understanding the role of AI in customer targeting, personalization, automation, and data-driven marketing strategies.</li>\n<li><strong>Application-Centric Learning: </strong>Real-world projects, case studies, and campaign-based assignments to build industry-ready skills.</li>\n<li><strong>Tools &amp; Platform Exposure: </strong>Training on digital platforms and tools used for analytics, advertising, and content management.</li>\n<li><strong> Ethics, Data Privacy &amp; Responsible Marketing: </strong>Focus on ethical marketing practices, data protection, and responsible use of digital and AI technologies.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its focus on <strong>practical and industry-oriented learning</strong>, where students actively engage in creating, managing, and analyzing digital campaigns. The curriculum is designed to bridge the gap between traditional marketing principles and modern digital practices enhanced by artificial intelligence.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Through a combination of conceptual understanding and hands-on experience, students develop the skills required to adapt to the dynamic digital landscape and evolving consumer trends.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the Department of Commerce, we aim to nurture professionals who are creative, analytically driven, and technologically equipped to excel in the field of digital marketing and business innovation.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-05-23 00:00:00'),
(1469, 188, 28, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Scientific &amp; Research-Oriented Curriculum:</strong> NEP-based curriculum covering Cognitive, Social, Developmental, and Applied Psychology along with Research Methodology and Statistics.</li>\n<li><strong>Academic Excellence with Analytical Focus:</strong> Delivered by experienced faculty with strong academic and research orientation, fostering critical thinking and conceptual clarity.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Well-Equipped Psychology Laboratory:</strong> Hands-on exposure to basic psychological testing, experimental methods, and behavioral observation techniques.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Practical &amp; Application-Based Learning:</strong> Use of case discussions, experiments, and structured activities to understand behavior in real-world contexts.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Research &amp; Data-Driven Approach:</strong> Focus on research design, data collection, analysis, and interpretation using statistical tools.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Understanding of Mental Health &amp; Human Behavior:</strong> Foundational insight into cognitive, emotional, and social aspects of human functioning.</li>\n<li><strong>Ethics &amp; Responsible Practice:</strong> Emphasis on ethical principles, confidentiality, and responsible conduct in academic and applied settings.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its focus on <strong>scientific inquiry and experiential learning</strong>, enabling students to observe, analyze, and interpret behavior using structured methodologies. The curriculum progresses from foundational concepts in the initial years to more advanced and research-oriented learning in the Honours year.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The programme is designed to prepare students for <strong>higher studies and specialized training in psychology and related fields</strong>, while developing strong analytical, research, and observational skills.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the Department of Psychology, we aim to nurture individuals who are intellectually curious, ethically responsible, and grounded in the scientific study of human behavior.</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-05-23 00:00:00'),
(1470, 188, 29, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Advanced &amp; Specialized Curriculum:</strong> Comprehensive coverage of Clinical Psychology, Psychopathology, Psychological Assessment, Psychotherapy, Counselling, and Research Methods.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Experienced Faculty &amp; Professional Orientation:</strong> Delivered by qualified faculty with expertise in clinical and applied psychology, ensuring a balance between academic rigor and practical training.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Well-Equipped Psychology Laboratory:</strong> Hands-on training in psychological testing, assessment tools, case analysis, and experimental methods.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Clinical Training &amp; Field Exposure:</strong> Structured internships and fieldwork in hospitals, mental health centers, NGOs, and related settings for supervised practical experience.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Practical &amp; Case-Based Learning:</strong> Exposure to case studies, diagnostic formulations, assessment techniques, and therapeutic approaches.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Research &amp; Dissertation: </strong>Strong emphasis on research methodology, data analysis, and dissertation work to develop scientific and investigative skills.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Ethics &amp; Professional Responsibility:</strong> Focus on ethical practices, confidentiality, and responsible conduct in clinical and research settings.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive feature of the programme is its emphasis on <strong>integrated academic and clinical training</strong>, where students engage in supervised practical work alongside theoretical learning. The programme encourages critical thinking, case-based analysis, and evidence-based approaches to understanding and addressing psychological concerns.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Through internships, fieldwork, and research activities, students gain meaningful exposure to real-world clinical environments. The programme is designed to prepare graduates for <strong>advanced training, supervised practice, and professional roles in mental health and related domains</strong>, in accordance with prevailing regulatory guidelines.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the Department of Psychology, we aim to develop competent, ethical, and reflective professionals equipped to contribute responsibly to the field of clinical psychology</p>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-05-23 00:00:00'),
(1471, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', '<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-4 mb-3\"><img class=\"img-fluid\" style=\"width: 100%; border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 5px;\" src=\"https://mnwc.edu.in/uploads/SAS.jpeg\" alt=\"B.Sc. Data Science with SAS\" /></div>\n<div class=\"col-md-8\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>B.Sc. Data Science with SAS</strong> is a future-focused undergraduate program designed to prepare students for careers in Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Business Analytics, and emerging digital technologies . Offered in collaboration with <strong>Maniben Nanavati Women&rsquo;s College (Autonomous)</strong>, the program blends academic excellence with industry-oriented training to create highly skilled and employable professionals.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-12\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The curriculum provides extensive exposure to industry-standard tools and technologies through hands-on learning, real-world datasets, live projects, and practical case studies. Students receive training in key areas such as Data Analytics, Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, Data Visualization, Python Programming, Business Intelligence, and Predictive Analytics.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The program offers more than <strong>315+ hours of specialized training</strong>, <strong>24&times;7 laboratory access</strong>, self-paced learning modules, and opportunities to earn globally recognized certifications. Regular interaction with industry experts, workshops, seminars, industrial visits, and internship support ensures students gain practical exposure to current industry trends and professional practices.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Following a <strong>3+1 year academic structure</strong>, the program is open to students from both Science and Commerce streams after HSC or equivalent qualification. The curriculum is designed to develop analytical thinking, problem-solving abilities, technical expertise, and business decision-making skills required in the modern digital economy.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduates can pursue rewarding career opportunities as Data Analysts, Business Analysts, Data Scientists, AI Specialists, Machine Learning Engineers, BI Developers, Financial Analysts, Healthcare Data Analysts, and Technology Consultants across sectors such as Information Technology, Banking &amp; Finance, Healthcare, Retail, E-commerce, Manufacturing, Cybersecurity, and Automation.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With a strong combination of academic knowledge, practical skills, industry certifications, and professional exposure, the B.Sc. Data Science with SAS program empowers students to become future-ready professionals and leaders in the rapidly evolving world of data and technology.<br /><br /><strong>About SAS: Data and AI Solutions<br /></strong>SAS is a global leader in data and AI, helping organizations make confident decisions with AI they can trust. For decades, SAS has set the standard for delivering software that drives meaningful impact, incorporating deep industry expertise, transparency, and governance. SAS gives you THE POWER TO KNOW&reg;.<strong><br /></strong></p>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 1, '', 0, 2, '2026-07-09 11:25:40');
